    ("executed-vector-groups-determine-modeled-service-cost", "simd-execution", "service-time", "predicts", "SIMD arithmetic execution predicts Active service time requirement under the declared serial instruction-cost model.", "For integer N>=0 independent valid element operations and usable integer vector width L>=1, the implementation executes K=floor(N/L) vector operations and r=N modulo L scalar tail operations, with fixed positive costs cv and cs; no setup, memory stall, loop-control work or overlap is modeled, giving service cost K*cv+r*cs rather than an automatic L-fold speedup", ""),
    ("dependent-addresses-limit-outstanding-demands", "dependent-loads", "memory-parallelism", "inhibits", "Serial dependent load chain inhibits Independent outstanding memory demands from that chain.", "The declared demand engine has capacity for at least two requests, but each next address in this chain of at least two loads is unknown until the previous response completes; no address/value prediction, software or hardware prefetch, or unrelated request stream is present, so this chain can keep at most one request outstanding", ""),
    ("independent-demands-enable-latency-overlap", "memory-parallelism", "wall-time", "predicts", "The set of Independent outstanding memory demands predicts Elapsed wall clock duration in the parallel fixed-latency model.", "The declared server accepts K>=2 independent requests at the same start time, can serve all K concurrently without bandwidth or queue contention, and each has fixed response latency D>0; issue overhead and other work are zero, so the batch completes in D rather than the K*D required by serial dependent issue", ""),
    ("dependent-miss-latency-sums-on-chain", "memory-latency", "wall-time", "predicts", "Demand memory service latency predicts Elapsed wall clock duration of the serialized miss chain.", "The declared pointer-chasing chain has K>=1 demand loads, every load misses to the same boundary with fixed latency D>0, each next address becomes available only on its predecessor's response, and no prefetch, overlap, cache hit or local processing cost intervenes; total duration is K*D", ""),
    ("line-size-determines-byte-offset", "line-granularity", "line-offset", "predicts", "Cache line byte granularity predicts Address offset within cache line under the declared address split.", "The abstract cache uses nonnegative integer byte address a and positive power-of-two line size L bytes with no address wrap or virtual-alias complication; the offset is a modulo L, independent of any universal real-processor line size", ""),
    ("ways-determine-capacity-with-fixed-geometry", "associativity", "cache-capacity", "predicts", "Cache set associativity predicts Configured cache data capacity for fixed set and line counts.", "The declared cache has S>=1 sets, A>=1 ways per set and L>=1 data bytes per line, all integers, with exactly A line slots per set and metadata excluded; data capacity is S*A*L bytes, so changing A while holding S and L fixed also changes capacity", ""),
    ("line-split-determines-set-index", "line-granularity", "set-index", "predicts", "Cache line byte granularity predicts Cache address set index in the modulo indexed model.", "For nonnegative integer byte address a, positive power-of-two L-byte lines and positive power-of-two S sets, the declared model selects block b=floor(a/L) and set b modulo S; no hardware hash, skewed indexing or translation-dependent synonym is included", ""),
    ("line-split-determines-tag", "line-granularity", "cache-tag", "predicts", "Cache line byte granularity predicts Cache line tag identity under the same explicit address model.", "The declared unbounded nonnegative byte-address model has L-byte lines and S sets, both positive powers of two, and uses set=floor(a/L) modulo S; the accompanying tag is floor(a/(L*S)), with no tag truncation or hidden address-space identifier", ""),
    ("empty-residency-causes-first-demand-miss", "cold-cache", "compulsory-miss", "causes", "Initially cold modeled cache causes Cold first reference cache miss on the specified demand.", "The declared cache begins empty, the next demand is the first reference to a valid line, and there is no prefetch, shared-cache insertion, earlier store allocation or bypass path that supplies it; the demand lookup precedes its normal fill", ""),
    ("fitting-repeated-scan-predicts-miss-fraction", "temporal-reuse", "l1-miss-rate", "predicts", "Repeated access to the same data predicts Level one local miss fraction for the fitting cyclic scan.", "The declared initially empty fully associative LRU level-one cache holds K>=W>=1 lines; a read-only demand trace scans the same W distinct lines in the same order for integer R>=2 passes, with fill on miss and no prefetch, invalidation or intervening traffic, giving W misses among R*W demands", ""),
    ("global-reuse-distance-predicts-eviction", "reuse-distance", "eviction", "predicts", "Distinct line reuse distance predicts Cache line eviction before the specified repeated access.", "In the declared fully associative K-line LRU cache with integer K>=1, the line was made most recently used by its prior access and at least K distinct other lines have since been demanded without another access to it; every miss fills, with no bypass, pinning, prefetch or invalidation modifying the stack model", ""),
    ("long-reuse-distance-predicts-capacity-miss", "reuse-distance", "capacity-miss", "predicts", "Distinct line reuse distance predicts Reference capacity cache miss at the next reference in the fully associative case.", "The modeled actual cache is the K-line fully associative LRU reference itself, integer K>=1, and the requested previously seen line has at least K distinct intervening lines since its last access; read-only demand filling has no prefetch or invalidation, so this is a noncompulsory miss rather than a set-conflict classification", ""),
    ("same-index-trace-predicts-conflict-miss", "set-index", "conflict-miss", "predicts", "Cache address set index predicts Set mapping conflict miss in the specified direct mapped trace.", "The declared initially empty direct-mapped cache has S>=2 sets and one line per set, index(block)=block modulo S, and read-only block trace [0,S,0]; the comparison cache is initially empty fully associative LRU with the same S-line capacity, with demand fills and no other traffic or prefetch", ""),
    ("different-tag-predicts-resident-eviction", "cache-tag", "eviction", "predicts", "Cache line tag identity predicts Cache line eviction for a completed conflicting fill.", "The declared one-way cache's selected set contains one valid resident tag, a demand for a different tag in that same set returns its valid line normally, and the allocate-on-miss controller admits it into that sole slot with no concurrent activity or bypass; the old resident cannot remain in that slot", ""),
    ("packed-spatial-use-reduces-line-transfer-bytes", "spatial-locality", "memory-traffic", "inhibits", "Nearby address access pattern inhibits Transferred memory boundary bytes in the stated packed layout comparison.", "The declared single read-only demand-filled cache is directly backed by DRAM, starts empty with capacity for at least one L-byte line, has no prefetch or other traffic, and fetches one full line from DRAM on every miss; N>=2 useful e-byte elements with e dividing L and 1<=e<L are accessed once, comparing aligned packed stride e with aligned stride L at the same DRAM boundary and no writes or writebacks", ""),
    ("cyclic-oversized-working-set-predicts-capacity-misses", "working-set", "capacity-miss", "predicts", "Accessed working set footprint predicts Reference capacity cache miss throughout later cycles of the specified trace.", "The declared actual/reference cache is initially empty fully associative K-line LRU, and a read-only trace repeatedly visits each of M distinct lines once in the same cyclic order with integers M>K>=1 and at least two cycles; every demand fills and there is no prefetch, bypass or invalidation, so each repeat has M-1 distinct intervening lines", ""),
    ("expanded-lru-capacity-avoids-fit-case-evictions", "cache-capacity", "eviction", "inhibits", "Configured cache data capacity inhibits Cache line eviction when expanded to fit the declared cyclic set.", "Compare initially empty fully associative LRU caches of M-1 and M whole lines for integer M>=2, unchanged line size and read-only trace of M distinct lines scanned twice in order; all demands allocate on miss with no other traffic, prefetch or invalidation, so this is a fixed-policy inclusion case rather than arbitrary hardware associativity tuning", ""),
    ("evicted-next-line-causes-local-miss", "eviction", "l1-miss-rate", "causes", "Cache line eviction causes Level one local miss fraction to increase in the one demand comparison.", "The declared level-one cache held the next requested line, the intervention evicts exactly that line before a measurement containing just its next demand, and no refill, prefetch or alternative cache insertion occurs before the lookup; the otherwise identical comparison retains it, so the observed fraction changes from zero to one", ""),
    ("local-miss-fraction-determines-blocking-amat", "l1-miss-rate", "mean-access-cost", "predicts", "Level one local miss fraction predicts Mean blocking memory access cost with conditional downstream misses.", "The declared serial blocking hierarchy charges h1>=0 on every demand, incremental h2>=0 only after a level-one miss and incremental D>=0 only after a level-two miss; m1 is in (0,1] and m2 in [0,1] is conditional on reaching level two, all costs use the same time unit, and no overlap is credited, giving h1+m1*(h2+m2*D)", ""),
    ("conditional-downstream-misses-determine-dram-bytes", "l2-miss-rate", "memory-traffic", "predicts", "Level two conditional miss fraction predicts Transferred memory boundary bytes after the two cache levels.", "The declared read-only two-level cache model records N>=1 original line demands, observed level-one fraction m1>0 and downstream local fraction m2 in [0,1] from their actual integer counts; each level-two miss independently fetches one uncoalesced L-byte line from DRAM with integer L>=1, and no prefetch, writeback, extra level or protocol byte overhead is counted, giving N*m1*m2*L bytes", ""),
    ("cache-warmup-reduces-measured-fit-case-cost", "warmup", "mean-access-cost", "inhibits", "Executed benchmark warmup phase inhibits Mean blocking memory access cost in the stated cache-only comparison.", "The abstract benchmark uses read-only demand allocation on every miss with no bypass, scans W>=1 distinct lines that fit its fully associative LRU cache, and warmup first demands all W and the identical measured scan follows immediately with no other traffic or invalidation; compare with a cold measured scan using fixed hit cost h and positive additional miss cost p, ignoring JIT, frequency and other effects", ""),
    ("associativity-can-worsen-specific-lru-trace", "associativity", "mean-access-cost", "predicts", "Cache set associativity predicts Mean blocking memory access cost for the specified equal capacity counterexample.", "Two initially empty two-line caches process read-only block trace [0,1,3,0]: one is direct mapped by block modulo 2, the other fully associative LRU; every read miss allocates and completes its fill with no bypass, prefetch or invalidation, and each lookup costs h plus positive penalty p only on a miss, giving respective means h+3*p/4 and h+p", ""),
    ("counter-state-determines-prior-prediction", "counter-state", "predicted-direction", "predicts", "Two bit predictor counter state predicts Predicted branch direction before the current update.", "The declared predictor has integer state c in {0,1,2,3}, predicts taken exactly when c>=2 and otherwise not taken, and reads that state before using the current branch's actual outcome; this is an explicit abstract policy rather than an Intel predictor specification", ""),
    ("resolved-outcomes-trigger-counter-updates", "branch-outcomes", "counter-update", "causes", "Actual branch outcome sequence causes Saturating predictor state update at each resolved event.", "The declared model resolves its supplied taken/not-taken outcomes in order and applies exactly one post-resolution counter update per event under its configured learning policy, with no speculative update, reset or skipped training event; the prediction for that event was already recorded", ""),
    ("saturating-rule-determines-next-counter", "counter-update", "counter-state", "predicts", "Saturating predictor state update predicts Two bit predictor counter state for the next lookup.", "The declared update starts from integer c in {0,1,2,3}, uses min(3,c+1) on a taken outcome and max(0,c-1) on a not-taken outcome, and no other writer intervenes; saturation retains an endpoint rather than wrapping from 3 to 0 or resetting to a fixed weak state", ""),
    ("saved-wrong-direction-predicts-mismatch", "predicted-direction", "misprediction", "predicts", "Predicted branch direction predicts Branch prediction mismatch for the specified contrary outcome.", "For one event in the declared model the saved pre-update prediction is taken, while the resolved program outcome is not taken; mismatch is assessed from that saved prediction and actual result, not from a newly recomputed prediction after the state update", ""),
    ("initial-state-changes-alternating-trace-errors", "cold-predictor", "misprediction", "predicts", "Declared initial predictor state predicts Branch prediction mismatch count for the alternating trace.", "One unaliased two-bit counter predicts taken at state>=2 and saturates up on taken/down on not-taken after each prediction; the exact trace [taken,not-taken] repeats R>=1 integer times with no resets, yielding R mismatches from initial state 0 but 2*R from initial state 1", ""),
    ("constant-taken-stream-has-initial-training-errors", "branch-outcomes", "misprediction", "predicts", "Actual branch outcome sequence predicts Branch prediction mismatch count for the stated training run.", "The declared one-entry predictor starts at state 0, predicts taken at state>=2 before updating and saturates upward after each actual taken result; the trace contains N>=1 integer taken outcomes and no other updates, so mismatch count is min(N,2), despite the stream's completely taken bias", ""),
    ("branch-address-mapping-predicts-entry-alias", "branch-site", "predictor-alias", "predicts", "Static conditional branch site predicts Shared predictor entry aliasing under the declared index function.", "The abstract tagless predictor has M>=1 integer entries indexed by floor(pc/4) modulo M; two distinct sites have byte addresses 4*q and 4*(q+M) for integer q>=0, so both consult the same entry, with no extra history hash or tag disambiguation", ""),
    ("opposed-aliased-branches-increase-errors", "predictor-alias", "misprediction", "causes", "Shared predictor entry aliasing causes Branch prediction mismatch growth in the opposed branch trace.", "In the declared two-bit model, site A is always taken and B always not taken, execution alternates A,B for R>=1 rounds, predictions precede saturating updates, and the comparison changes separate counters initially at 1 to one shared counter initially at 1; no other branches, resets or predictor mechanisms intervene", ""),
    ("wrong-prediction-triggers-recovery", "misprediction", "recovery-work", "causes", "Branch prediction mismatch causes Misprediction recovery work in the specified speculative pipeline.", "The declared single-path speculative pipeline used its guess to issue at least one wrong-path operation before branch resolution, and its correct-execution policy cancels that speculative path and redirects to the resolved target; no dual-path execution or earlier resolution avoided this recovery case", ""),
    ("recovery-count-determines-service-cost", "recovery-work", "service-time", "predicts", "Misprediction recovery work predicts Active service time requirement in the fixed penalty model.", "The declared serial pipeline's otherwise unchanged operation costs B>=0 time units excluding recovery, incurs M>=0 actual mismatches each with fixed incremental penalty r>0 in those same units, and none overlaps or replaces another critical cost; modeled service time is B+M*r, not a universal hardware misprediction formula", ""),
    ("removed-branch-eliminates-its-mispredictions", "branchless-selection", "misprediction", "prevents", "Branchless value selection prevents Branch prediction mismatch at the eliminated branch site.", "The declared legal lowering replaces this conditional branch by supported nonbranching value-selection operations, and the final executed instruction sequence has no conditional branch at that site or replacement branch serving the same selection; predictions and mismatches at unrelated remaining branches are outside the claim", ""),
    ("eager-branchless-arms-add-unconditional-work", "branchless-selection", "extra-work", "causes", "Branchless value selection causes Additional unconditional computation in the eager two arm implementation.", "The declared original branch executes exactly one of two distinct positive-work candidate expressions; the legal branchless implementation evaluates both total nonthrowing effect-free expressions and selects their value, without constant folding, common-subexpression merging or another removal of the previously skipped expression", ""),
    ("extra-serial-computation-adds-cpu-time", "extra-work", "cpu-time", "predicts", "Additional unconditional computation predicts Aggregate CPU execution time increase in the serial cost model.", "One measured thread performs K>=1 added operations at fixed positive CPU cost c per operation, all other work remains unchanged, and there is no instruction overlap, rematerialization saving or previously charged stall that the new work replaces; the modeled extra CPU time is K*c, separately from any branch-recovery saving", ""),
    ("taken-warmup-trains-declared-counter", "warmup", "counter-state", "causes", "Executed benchmark warmup phase causes Two bit predictor counter state to reach its taken endpoint in this model.", "The abstract benchmark predictor starts one counter at 0, uses post-outcome saturating increments for taken branches, and warmup actually resolves at least three taken outcomes at that site before measurement; no other aliased branch, reset or intervening update changes the entry between phases", ""),
    ("branchless-cost-includes-both-candidates", "branchless-selection", "service-time", "predicts", "Branchless value selection predicts Active service time requirement in the declared eager cost comparison.", "The serial model evaluates two independent total candidate expressions costing a>0 and b>0 and a supported select costing s>=0, with no overlap or other work, so its branchless service cost is a+b+s; the comparison branch executes one candidate and has separately specified branch/recovery costs, so branch removal alone does not determine which implementation wins", ""),
    ("per-operation-allocation-and-throughput-determine-rate", "allocation-per-op", "allocation-rate", "predicts", "Materialized allocation bytes per operation predicts Materialized allocation byte rate with matching throughput.", "The declared measurement attributes B allocated bytes to N>0 completed operations over the same T>0 seconds, excludes unrelated background allocations and source allocations optimized away, and uses b=B/N with throughput X=N/T; allocation rate is b*X=B/T bytes/s, not b alone", ""),
    ("sufficient-fast-capacity-avoids-demand-refill", "allocator-fastpath", "allocator-refill", "prevents", "Available allocator fast path prevents Allocator backing capacity refill for the qualified request.", "The declared OSTEP-style allocator already has an eligible block satisfying this request's full size/alignment requirements, follows a demand-refill-only policy and has no concurrent consumer, eager replenishment or other refill obligation; its successful local bookkeeping path therefore needs no backing refill for this request", ""),
    ("mapping-refill-enters-kernel-service", "allocator-refill", "syscall-entry", "causes", "Allocator backing capacity refill causes System call kernel entry under the selected mapping policy.", "In the declared OSTEP 1.10 Unix-style model the refill path has no reusable managed region and calls the OS mapping service through its trap interface, with normal dispatch and no user-space interception; this is the chosen external refill case, not a claim that every malloc or refill policy must issue a syscall", ""),
    ("syscall-dispatch-performs-kernel-work", "syscall-entry", "kernel-work", "causes", "System call kernel entry causes System call service work through the selected dispatcher.", "The OSTEP 1.10 limited-direct-execution model transfers a valid service request through the configured trap handler and dispatches its normal kernel service path; the current task can remain scheduled throughout and return without a switch to another thread", ""),
    ("unresolved-block-selects-another-runnable-thread", "blocking-operation", "context-switch", "causes", "Thread blocking operation causes Scheduled thread context switch under the stated scheduler conditions.", "The declared work-conserving single-CPU scheduler reaches its next selection while the current thread's blocking condition remains unresolved and another thread is runnable; normal scheduler progress occurs and no wake-before-selection lets the blocked thread continue immediately", ""),
    ("switch-routine-restores-next-context", "context-switch", "context-work", "causes", "Scheduled thread context switch causes Thread context restoration work in the selected routine.", "The declared OSTEP-style switch changes to a distinct runnable thread and uses the specified save/stack-switch/restore routine for its required register state; this does not prescribe every architecture's register set or imply that every switch flushes all cache and TLB state", ""),
    ("context-work-adds-accounted-cpu-time", "context-work", "cpu-time", "predicts", "Thread context restoration work predicts Aggregate CPU execution time in the explicit cost ledger.", "The declared CPU accounting model includes kernel switch execution, charges fixed c>0 time units for each of M>=0 integer switches in addition to unchanged body work B>=0, and credits no overlap or offsetting saved work; the accounted total is B+M*c, rather than a universal OS per-thread accounting rule", ""),
    ("batch-capacity-determines-successful-entry-count", "batch-size", "entry-count", "predicts", "System call batch capacity predicts Executed kernel entry count under the successful batching policy.", "The declared caller submits N>=0 logical requests in full batches of integer capacity b>=1 plus one final nonempty partial batch if needed; each batch uses exactly one successful syscall, all items are accepted, and no empty calls, partial acceptance, retries, signals or other entries are counted, giving ceil(N/b)", ""),
    ("entry-count-determines-kernel-overhead-work", "entry-count", "kernel-work", "predicts", "Executed kernel entry count predicts System call service work in the additive batch cost model.", "For the same completed N-item workload, the declared successful service charges fixed entry/exit overhead h>0 per syscall and item processing cost c>=0 per item, with no blocking, retries or overlap in this cost ledger; E entries therefore cost E*h+N*c in matching units", ""),
    ("batch-hold-adds-unoverlapped-request-latency", "batch-wait", "latency", "causes", "Added batch formation wait causes Request response latency growth in the isolated hold comparison.", "The declared request is ready when the batching controller holds it for w>0 time units, its downstream service would otherwise be immediately available, and that hold neither overlaps nor replaces another wait; all downstream elapsed costs and completion semantics remain unchanged between comparisons, so the extra critical delay is w", ""),
    ("insufficient-budget-triggers-declared-collection", "heap-headroom", "collection-work", "predicts", "Remaining allocation headroom budget predicts Triggered collection processing work at the declared threshold crossing.", "The abstract runtime has remaining budget H>=0, receives a valid allocation request a>H, and its explicit policy schedules and executes a collection before retrying this allocation with normal collector progress; the claim is that work is triggered, not that collection must reclaim enough memory or prevent failure", ""),
    ("stop-the-world-work-delays-ready-request", "collection-work", "latency", "causes", "Triggered collection processing work causes Request response latency growth in the stated pause model.", "The declared collector stops the required mutator for a positive pause P, the measured request is already pending and otherwise ready at pause start, and cannot finish through another thread while paused; the entire pause lies on its critical path with no overlapped wait, and all remaining costs are unchanged", ""),
    ("removed-allocation-reduces-materialized-bytes", "allocation-elimination", "allocation-per-op", "inhibits", "Compiler removal of allocation work inhibits Materialized allocation bytes per operation for the specified object.", "A semantics-preserving optimizer has eliminated one otherwise materialized a>0 byte allocation per completed logical operation, preserves the same workload/output contract and introduces no replacement allocation; the measurement counts actual allocations for those operations rather than source-level new expressions or retained heap size", ""),
    ("userspace-fast-path-avoids-allocation-syscall", "allocator-fastpath", "syscall-entry", "prevents", "Available allocator fast path prevents System call kernel entry in the specified local allocation path.", "The declared single-thread allocator satisfies the valid request from existing managed capacity using only its user-space metadata path, with no refill, locking syscall, logging or other service call in that path; a later demand-page fault or payload initialization is not being equated with an allocation syscall", ""),
    ("constant-allocation-rate-consumes-budget", "allocation-rate", "heap-headroom", "predicts", "Materialized allocation byte rate predicts Remaining allocation headroom budget in the declared fluid approximation.", "The explicit continuous-byte budget model starts with H0>0 bytes, consumes allocation budget at constant r>0 bytes/s, and has no reclamation, reuse or refill before its threshold; for 0<=t<=H0/r the remaining modeled budget is H0-r*t, whereas a real bursty sequence with only the same average rate need not reach its trigger at that time", ""),
    ("sample-event-records-profile-observation", "sample-event", "profile", "causes", "Profile sampling event causes Collected execution profile record creation under the declared recorder policy.", "The configured sampler handles the event, obtains the requested time/event/stack fields successfully and its recorder appends one record with no loss or filtering; the record describes that sampling population and does not automatically measure every instruction or off-CPU wait", ""),
    ("uniform-cpu-samples-predict-expected-self-attribution", "cpu-time-sampling", "self-cost", "predicts", "Uniform CPU time sampling model predicts Leaf self sampled attribution expectation for the stated region.", "The ideal model takes n>=1 independent points uniformly over a fixed running-CPU-time interval, region R is the actual leaf for fraction p in [0,1], and stacks are attributed without loss or skid; expected self count is n*p, while one finite sample's realized count need not equal it", ""),
    ("recorded-stacks-determine-inclusive-count", "profile", "inclusive-cost", "predicts", "Collected execution profile predicts Inclusive sampled frame attribution under the explicit presence rule.", "The supplied profile is a finite list of accurately labeled stack samples with unit weight, and the declared aggregation counts a selected frame identifier once per sample whenever it appears anywhere in that sample's stack; ancestor and descendant inclusive totals can overlap and must not be summed as disjoint time", ""),
    ("recorded-leaves-determine-self-count", "profile", "self-cost", "predicts", "Collected execution profile predicts Leaf self sampled attribution under the stated leaf rule.", "Each retained unit-weight sample has one identified executing leaf and its caller stack, and this report assigns self count only to that leaf; unlike inclusive attribution, a caller receives no self credit from a sample whose executing leaf is its descendant", ""),
    ("dominant-self-count-identifies-estimated-hotspot", "self-cost", "hotspot", "predicts", "Leaf self sampled attribution predicts Estimated CPU execution hotspot under the declared ranking policy.", "The analyzer ranks nonoverlapping leaf counts from n>0 same-mode samples, one region R owns more than n/2 of them, and the configured report marks the largest self-count region as its estimated hotspot; this is a report from the sampled population, not proof of end-to-end critical-path importance", ""),
    ("measured-hotspot-enables-targeted-hypothesis", "hotspot", "bottleneck-hypothesis", "enables", "Estimated CPU execution hotspot enables Workload specific bottleneck hypothesis formation as a candidate for testing.", "The declared diagnosis procedure uses the measured region as an evidence-motivated candidate only when independent workload knowledge places that CPU work on the response path and indicates CPU-bound service; it still requires a controlled intervention before claiming that changing the region improves overall performance", ""),
    ("unoverlapped-offcpu-wait-adds-response-delay", "offcpu-wait", "latency", "causes", "Critical path off CPU wait causes Request response latency increase in the isolated wait model.", "The request cannot progress through another thread during this positive wait, the interval does not overlap or replace an already-required wait or independent work, and the remaining service/response costs are unchanged; this adds elapsed latency without charging running CPU time to the waiting thread", ""),
    ("instrumentation-cost-adds-accounted-cpu-time", "measurement-overhead", "cpu-time", "predicts", "Profiling instrumentation perturbation predicts Aggregate CPU execution time increase in the declared additive case.", "The measurement inserts K>=1 executed instrumentation operations at fixed positive CPU cost c each on the accounted thread, preserves all original body work, and has no overlapping or removed work in this serial cost model; measured CPU time includes K*c extra even though the intended application workload is unchanged", ""),
    ("matched-samples-enable-timing-comparison", "timing-samples", "controlled-comparison", "enables", "The set of Observed benchmark timing samples enables Matched implementation timing comparison when the accompanying controls hold.", "The retained records contain completed baseline and candidate timings for the same verified workload, operation unit and start/stop boundary, with relevant environment fixed or appropriately balanced and failures identified separately; those records support an actual timing comparison without claiming that a single favorable ratio proves a universal improvement", ""),
    ("synchronous-sampling-adds-observation-work", "sample-event", "measurement-overhead", "causes", "Profile sampling event causes Profiling instrumentation perturbation in the synchronous handler model.", "The declared sampling policy interrupts the profiled execution to run a positive-work capture/record handler on that same CPU before resumption, with no eliminated body work or overlap hiding its cost; hardware offload or another observation mode is a different model", ""),
    ("resolved-harness-configuration-runs-warmup", "harness", "warmup", "causes", "Configured benchmark harness causes Executed benchmark warmup phase under the positive warmup configuration.", "OpenJDK JMH 1.37 has resolved a configuration with a positive warmup-iteration count and valid benchmark method, the fork starts normally and benchmark invocations complete without abort; the count names warmup iterations rather than promising exactly that many individual method invocations or a stationary outcome", ""),
    ("resolved-harness-records-measurement-phase", "harness", "measurement-phase", "causes", "Configured benchmark harness causes Recorded benchmark measurement phase execution after its setup policy.", "OpenJDK JMH 1.37 has a positive configured measurement-iteration count, setup and any requested warmup complete normally, and the measured benchmark invocations and iterations complete normally without exception, abort or timeout; these completed measurement iterations supply its reported statistics rather than automatically including every preceding setup and warmup cost", ""),
    ("profiled-warmup-creates-process-history", "warmup", "profile-pollution", "causes", "Executed benchmark warmup phase causes Shared JVM optimization profile history accumulation in the profiling runtime case.", "The chosen optimizing JVM used by JMH 1.37 records the warmup invocations' receiver/count feedback under its active profiling policy and reuses the same JVM for the next measurement without resetting that feedback; this is not a promise that an interpreter-only or differently configured runtime performs the same JIT activity", ""),
    ("fresh-fork-excludes-previous-jvm-profile-state", "fork-isolation", "profile-pollution", "prevents", "Fresh benchmark JVM fork prevents Shared JVM optimization profile history reuse from the earlier JVM process.", "OpenJDK JMH 1.37 starts a genuinely separate benchmark JVM instead of reusing the previous benchmark process, its feedback state is process-local and no persistent profile import restores the earlier history; the child still develops its own profiles, and host caches, predictor, frequency and external load are not reset by this condition", ""),
    ("required-result-blocks-trivial-dead-work-removal", "result-use", "dead-work-removal", "prevents", "Required benchmark result consumption prevents Unused benchmark work elimination of the necessary value computation.", "The selected JMH 1.37 return/sink path makes the computed value relevant under its compiler contract, runtime inputs require the corresponding result, and the proposed deletion supplies no equivalent replacement; this blocks deletion merely because the result was ignored, not valid folding, hoisting or another equivalent implementation", ""),
