    ("deleted-unused-work-reduces-modeled-service", "dead-work-removal", "service-time", "inhibits", "Unused benchmark work elimination inhibits Active service time requirement for the deleted work in this model.", "The optimizer legitimately deletes K>=1 executed positive-cost operations whose results/effects were unnecessary, the serial comparison charges c>0 per removed operation, and no replacement or other cost is added; the reduced measured body cost does not establish that the benchmark still represents the user's intended algorithmic task", ""),
    ("operation-credit-determines-throughput-units", "operation-normalization", "throughput", "predicts", "Declared operations per invocation predicts Completed operation throughput when the declaration matches real work.", "OpenJDK JMH 1.37 throughput accounting is considered for one benchmark thread with batchSize=1, I completed invocations over matching T>0 seconds and resolved positive integer operationsPerInvocation k; each invocation truly completes exactly k operations of the declared workload contract, giving k*I/T operations/s rather than treating the annotation as proof that work occurred", ""),
    ("floor-timer-resolution-bounds-interval-error", "timer-resolution", "timer-error", "predicts", "Elapsed timer quantization interval predicts Quantized elapsed measurement error bound for the floor timestamp model.", "The declared monotonic nonwrapping timer reports q(t)=delta*floor(t/delta) for delta>0 and finite 0<=t0<=t1; measured duration is q(t1)-q(t0), so its signed error relative to t1-t0 lies strictly between -delta and delta, without asserting that a real JMH clock follows this exact quantizer", ""),
    ("competing-cpu-service-perturbs-timing-samples", "external-noise", "timing-samples", "causes", "External benchmark timing interference causes Observed benchmark timing samples to include the added scheduling delay.", "In the declared single-CPU comparison, another runnable task preempts an otherwise-ready CPU-bound benchmark for q_i>=0 time during trial i, no useful benchmark progress or prior wait overlaps that service, and all other costs remain fixed; the observed duration includes q_i beyond the baseline, which can vary across trials or remain a systematic offset", ""),
    ("iid-stable-regime-gives-variance-estimator-expectation", "stationarity", "sample-variance", "predicts", "Stable measurement regime assumption predicts Observed timing sample variance expectation under the additional sampling hypotheses.", "The declared n>=2 timing observations are independent identically distributed real variables with common finite mean and variance sigma_squared, and the estimator uses sum((x_i-xbar)**2)/(n-1); its expectation is sigma_squared, while stationarity alone without independence does not supply this result", ""),
